class Solution {
    public String rankTeams(String[] votes) {
        Map<Character, int[]> rankMap = new HashMap<>();
        int n = votes[0].length();
        for(String vote : votes){
            for(int i=0; i < vote.length(); i++){
                char team = vote.charAt(i);
                rankMap.computeIfAbsent(team, k -> new int[n]);
                rankMap.get(team)[i]++;
            }
        }
        List<Character> teams = new ArrayList<>(rankMap.keySet());
        Collections.sort(teams, (a,b) -> {
            int[] array1 = rankMap.get(a);
            int[] array2 = rankMap.get(b);
            for(int i=0; i < n; i++){
                if(array1[i] != array2[i])
                   return array2[i] - array1[i];
            }
            return a-b; 
        });
        StringBuilder sb = new StringBuilder();
        for(Character c : teams){
            sb.append(c);
        }
        return String.valueOf(sb);
    }
}

time : O(votes * teams) + O(teams * log teams)
since team will be max from A to z 26 chars 
so it will be constant
total time : O(votes)

Space : 
rankMap stores votes in a T × T matrix
Each team stores an int[T] frequency array.
Worst case 26 teams × 26 positions:
O(T²) → constant max = 26×26 = 676 ints → negligible.
Other space
teams list = T → O(T)
Output string = T → O(T)
So total:
⭐ Space: O(T²) ≈ O(1) constant upper bound
Since T ≤ 26, this is constant space.
